# Chip Estimate Integrity — Phase E: Packing room floors (CORE)
#
# ACCEPTANCE CONTRACT (locked before Phase E implementation edits)
# E1 GIVEN a room classified as kitchen, garage, bedroom, or bathroom, WHEN its
#    work is estimated, THEN the LOCKED-pending-calibration minimum is applied
#    once to the aggregate ROOM before splitting: kitchen 150, garage 120,
#    bedroom 60, bathroom 30 minutes. Two rooms each receive their own floor.
# E2 GIVEN a room whose item-derived work exceeds its room-type floor, WHEN the
#    plan is generated, THEN item-derived minutes win; the floor never replaces
#    or adds to greater work.
# E3 GIVEN a floor-adjusted room workload, WHEN sessions are constructed, THEN
#    the adjusted room total is split into approximately 40-minute sessions and
#    the sum of those pre-compression session minutes exactly preserves the
#    adjusted room total (subject only to the existing 20-minute generic minimum
#    for room types without a larger floor).
# E4 GIVEN a kitchen with sparse, one-sided, or large-item work, WHEN room drafts
#    are built, THEN its 150-minute room floor is applied once across essential
#    and non-essential variants and it has at least two sessions before timeline
#    compression. A short timeline may merge those drafts under existing rules.
# E5 GIVEN normal and short timelines, WHEN a plan is generated, THEN locked room
#    ordering, first-night isolation, merge item coverage, completion continuity,
#    and reflow behavior remain intact. CORE tests, fresh validation, and walked
#    diffs pass. No deploy or reseed occurs.
